A.misconception('MIS-18','Parallel resistors do not combine by direct series addition.','Their shared voltage and added branch currents require the reciprocal rule.','Two 6 Ω branches across 6 V each carry 1 A, so total current is 2 A and total resistance is 3 Ω. Directly adding them would give 12 Ω and contradict the two-path current. The smaller-than-each-branch check helps reveal the topology confusion.','Two 6 Ω resistors are connected in parallel. Explain why their total is not 12 Ω and give the correct value.','The error uses series addition for two paths sharing the same voltage.~The reciprocal rule gives 3 Ω, smaller than either branch.')
