C('5.2.4-02','Which condition is required for the stated ohmic relation?',('Fixed temperature and physical conditions','Resistance must remain constant in the comparison.'),('A steadily heating filament','Its resistance changes.'),('A different material at every reading','That changes the conductor.'),('No current measurement','The relation involves current.'))
C('5.3-05','Parallel branches share what?',('Potential difference','They span the same two nodes.'),('Equal current regardless of components','Branch resistances can differ.'),('Equal resistance by definition','Components need not match.'),('A series-only path','Parallel creates separate paths.'))
C('5.3-10-M03','What does a relay use to operate contacts?',('An electromagnet','Its coil attracts an armature.'),('A melting link for each normal switch action','That describes destructive fuse action.'),('A permanently open air gap with no mechanism','A mechanism is needed.'),('A changing colour alone','Colour is not the switching force.'))
C('5.2.4-06-M02','Why does a filament lamp become non-ohmic during a voltage sweep?',('Its temperature and resistance change','Heating changes the current-voltage ratio.'),('Charge is used up','Charge is conserved.'),('Its length must vanish','No such change occurs.'),('The current has no energy transfer','The lamp receives energy.'))
C('5.3-01-M05','Which symbol identifies an ammeter?',('A in a circle','It is the current-measuring instrument.'),('V in a circle','That is a voltmeter.'),('Unequal parallel plates','That is a cell.'),('A circle with a cross','That is a lamp.'))
C('ANNEX.D-01','What is a diode’s rectifying behaviour?',('Strongly favours one direction','Its characteristic is asymmetric.'),('Equal constant resistance both ways','That is not the basic diode behaviour.'),('Creates charge','It does not create charge.'),('Measures mass directly','That is unrelated.'))
C('5.2.4-04','What resistance gives 6 V at 0.5 A?',('12 Ω','Use V/I.'),('3 Ω','This multiplies V and I.'),('0.083 Ω','This reverses the ratio.'),('6 Ω','This ignores current.'))
C('5.3-07-M01','What is 5 Ω in series with 8 Ω?',('13 Ω','Series resistances add.'),('3.08 Ω','This is their parallel combination.'),('40 Ω','This multiplies without dividing.'),('3 Ω','This subtracts.'))
C('5.3-07-M02','What is 4 Ω in parallel with 4 Ω?',('2 Ω','Equal parallel branches halve resistance.'),('8 Ω','That is series addition.'),('4 Ω','The second path increases conductance.'),('16 Ω','This multiplies branch values.'))
C('5.3-03','Two branches carry 0.2 A and 0.6 A. What source current feeds them?',('0.8 A','Branch currents add.'),('0.4 A','This subtracts rather than adds.'),('0.12 A','This multiplies currents.'),('3 A','This divides them.'))
C('5.2.3-02-M02','A wire’s diameter doubles at unchanged length, material and temperature. What is its resistance factor?',('One quarter','Area rises by four.'),('One half','This mistakes diameter for area.'),('Two','A thicker wire has lower resistance.'),('Four','This reverses the area dependence.'))
